}(x)$ treat the size of its input $x$?","options":["It returns the size $|x|$ and drops the sign","It discards the size, keeping only the sign","It keeps $x$ when $|x|\\le1$ and clips larger inputs to $\\pm1$","It shrinks $x$ proportionally, so larger inputs give larger outputs"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"9ec46b81a52521fe6711e2ee","time_limit":30},{"id":"signum_function_new_016_curated20261027_005","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"For which real numbers $x$ and $y$ does $\\operatorname{sgn}(xy)=\\operatorname{sgn}(x)\\,\\operatorname{sgn}(y)$ hold?","options":["For all real $x$ and $y$","Only when $x\\neq0$ and $y\\neq0$","Only when $x$ and $y$ have the same sign","Only when $x>0$ and $y>0$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"7a74337c5ddefa42c4c287fe","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_signum_function_5799e175_topup20261028_001","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Find the solution set in $\\mathbb{R}$ of the equation $\\operatorname{sgn}(x^2-4)=-1$.","options":["$[-2,2]$","$(-\\infty,-2)\\cup(2,\\infty)$","$(-2,2)$","$\\{-\\sqrt{3},\\sqrt{3}\\}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"18b2bd9ed00631421ca71a2a","time_limit":30}]}}